From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] deckcraft: the transliteration's walk, pieces and write as functions (plugin text map)

Phase 7 WP13 (docs/phase7/PLAN.md WP13, docs/plugins.md section 6a): the plugin text map of slides-plugins must walk exactly what
the transliteration commands walk and write back the way they do, so a plugin's result equals the built-in's. No behaviour
change of the commands: `pieces` is built on a new `cut` (the pieces with "inside the range" and "plain text" kept apart, which
the map needs for its flags), and the scope resolution moves into `resolve`. New: `text_scope` (the scope, kept from a read to its
write), `text_pieces` (every paragraph's pieces, in the commands' order) and `write_pieces` (new piece texts written as the
commands write theirs: runs, `normalize`, the selected range kept on the same text; one `Session::edit`). Our module (0120).
---

